// Build-only TypeScript config, wired in through `typescript.tsconfigPath` in
// next.config.js. tsconfig.json stays the full one — the config the editor and
// `npm run typecheck` use — so tests remain type-checked in CI.
//
// Why the split: tsconfig.json includes `**/*.ts`, which drags portfolio/tests/**
// into the build's type check. Those tests import outside portfolio/:
//
//   tests/integration/**              -> ../../../../testing/integration/fixtures
//   tests/integration/views.recording -> ../../../worker/workers/views.worker
//
// portfolio/Dockerfile copies only packages/{database,queues,templates,web3} and
// portfolio/. Neither testing/ nor worker/ ends up in the image, so tsc fails with
// TS2307 inside the container during `next build` — while CI, which checks out the
// whole repo, resolves those paths and passes green.
//
// Test files never reach the bundle either, so the production build has no reason
// to type-check them. If a new test lands outside tests/, add its pattern here.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "tests/**",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.test.tsx",
    "**/__tests__/**",
    "playwright.config.ts"
  ]
}